  "keyTakeaways": [
    "U.S. Chapter 38 exports slipped 2.8% to $36.19B in 2025; diagnostic and laboratory reagents (3822, $11.20B) grew 4.4% while biodiesel (3826) fell 60.4% and doped silicon wafers (3818) 16.3%.",
    "Canada, Mexico, South Korea and Singapore charge nothing on qualifying U.S. goods, and the EU, the largest market at $8.32B, has charged nothing since July 1, 2026 except on 3809.10 and 3824.60.",
    "China is the only large buyer that raised tariffs — a 10% extra duty on all U.S. goods — and exports there fell 21.3% to $2.59B; watch December 31, 2026 (its exclusions end) and January 10, 2027 (its 24-point suspension ends).",
    "Pesticides (3808, $4.49B) need registration in each market and, if not registered in the U.S., an EPA foreign purchaser acknowledgement before export; Brazil, their second-largest market, charges up to 14%."
  ],
